  "response": "```python\nx = 1\nresult = x << 3\nprint(result)\n```\n\nThis code will output **8**.\n\nHere's why:\n\n*  `<<` is the left shift operator in Python. It shifts the bits of a number to the left by a specified number of positions.\n* When you shift a number one position to the left, it's equivalent to multiplying it by 2.\n* So, `x << 3` (shifting 1 left by 3 positions) is the same as: 1 * 2 * 2 * 2 = 8.  \n\n\n\nLet me know if you have any other Python questions!",
